00:06:39.971 --> 00:06:46.511
A cyber security firm used OpenAI's Codex coding agent in a case circulating on X to uncover

00:06:46.511 --> 00:06:51.851
a critical security flaw in Java, one of the world's most widely used programming languages

00:06:51.851 --> 00:06:56.991
in about an hour, then built a working attack in about two more hours for less than $200

00:06:56.991 --> 00:06:58.391
in computing costs.

00:06:58.931 --> 00:07:05.411
The flaw, dubbed Java 4 Shell, sits in Java's base 64 decoder and can be triggered by sending

00:07:05.411 --> 00:07:10.851
just 64 A characters followed by a single equal sign, potentially corrupting computer

00:07:10.851 --> 00:07:15.071
memory and letting an attacker take over a server or expose sensitive data.

00:07:15.751 --> 00:07:21.191
Calif rated at 9.2 out of 10 for severity and demonstrated a working break-in on

00:07:21.191 --> 00:07:26.511
key cloak, a widely used login system, while noting that JIRA, Confluence, and

00:07:26.511 --> 00:07:32.731
Jenkins are also at risk. Java runs at 90% of Fortune 500 companies and is used

00:07:32.731 --> 00:07:37.951
by banks, hospitals, and governments worldwide. Oracle and OpenJDK have

00:07:37.951 --> 00:07:42.831
released fixes, and access to the agent is through OpenAI's API at Standard

00:07:42.831 --> 00:07:48.271
usage rates. I have no financial relationship with OpenAI or any other tool name today,

00:07:48.791 --> 00:07:52.391
and the concrete step is a natural language query against a code base.

00:07:52.991 --> 00:07:57.731
The same style of question you ask a segment footnote when you want the data lines growth versus

00:07:57.731 --> 00:08:04.337
the blend. Kinsis is expanding chip substrate capacity dedicated to NVIDIA by more than three

00:08:04.337 --> 00:08:10.937
and a half times, with production starting in the second half of 2027. SPIL is executing a

00:08:10.937 --> 00:08:16.117
