00:11:18.596 --> 00:11:24.376
release, even as reported earnings decline. Do you treat that tape as a re-rating or as

00:11:24.376 --> 00:11:26.456
a head-fake caused by acquisition noise.

00:11:27.196 --> 00:11:29.636
Sit with that for a second before you open the footnote.

00:11:30.216 --> 00:11:34.756
Once a single segment's revenue exceeds half the total and grows faster than the legacy

00:11:34.756 --> 00:11:40.236
businesses, analysts re-weight the multiple toward that segment's peer group, which often

00:11:40.236 --> 00:11:41.156
trades at a premium.

00:11:41.856 --> 00:11:47.596
In TMX's September quarter, the data and analytics line lifted overall receipts, while organic

00:11:47.596 --> 00:11:53.416
volumes also rose, yet operating expenses climbed because of acquisition and integration costs.

00:11:53.416 --> 00:11:58.156
So the market applied a blended multiple that reflected both the higher growth segment

00:11:58.156 --> 00:12:03.776
and the temporary cost drag. A practical check is to compare the data segments contribution

00:12:03.776 --> 00:12:09.376
margin against the trading segments margin in the same filing. When that gap widens, the

00:12:09.376 --> 00:12:14.476
stock tends to re-rate upward even if headline earnings are flat. The common misconception

00:12:14.476 --> 00:12:19.856
is that all revenue lines inside an exchange are interchangeable, as if a dollar of trading

00:12:19.856 --> 00:12:23.496
fees and a dollar of recurring data were the same quality of cash.

00:12:23.996 --> 00:12:28.636
When a segment that previously contributed less than 40% of revenue suddenly accounts

00:12:28.636 --> 00:12:33.976
for more than half and grows at double the rate of the legacy trading business, the valuation

00:12:33.976 --> 00:12:38.176
lens shifts from exchange multiples towards software and data multiples.

00:12:38.896 --> 00:12:44.096
Investors who keep applying the old blended multiple after that crossover miss the re-rating

00:12:44.096 --> 00:12:47.236
that occurs once the market recognizes the new revenue mix.

00:12:47.236 --> 00:12:52.776
The fix is to isolate the fastest growing segments growth rate in margin before deciding

00:12:52.776 --> 00:12:56.816
whether the current multiple is cheap or rich relative to that segment's peers.

00:12:57.476 --> 00:13:02.596
Open the most recent quarterly report, locate the segment footnote, record the data and

00:13:02.596 --> 00:13:07.696
analytics line as a percentage of total revenue, and compare its year-over-year growth rate

00:13:07.696 --> 00:13:11.016
to the trading and clearing lines before you form any price target.

00:13:11.476 --> 00:13:12.376
That is the homework.

00:13:12.376 --> 00:13:17.256
Pull TMX Group's latest quarterly segment breakdown on your brokerage platform,

00:13:17.776 --> 00:13:21.036
and check whether data now exceeds 50% of total revenue.

